write(B/'source-review.json',{'section':466,'changed_or_new_sources':{p:pin(p)for p in sources},'review':'Qt takeCentralWidget transfers the one original PlayerWorkspace into the retained shared ToolPage. MainWindow keeps an explicit stable workspace field for its existing16 routes; ordinary show after transfer returns the shared host, diagnostic layout remains attached to its main window. Operator/chat shortcuts select the group without resetting its child; actual form instances and drafts remain. Original back shortcut is parented to the movable workspace. A header action invokes the original workspace history; host history retains cross-reader reading. Only chat uses ignored vertical size hints so hidden pages do not force its minimum height; other pages retain scrolling. Existing pinned superqt QCollapsible hides connection controls; original backend callbacks, credentials and protocol fields are reused, relevant rows follow the mode. Expanded height is recomputed after mode changes; default collapsed content is explicitly set to zero. No new retries, catches, side-effect validation or private persistence.','whole_program_review_complete':False})
